deb-harden-ssh (1.0.0-1) stable; urgency=low

  * Initial release of deb-harden-ssh.
  * Add hardened OpenSSH server hardening drop-ins for access control,
    session timeouts, forwarding restrictions, and cryptographic defaults.
  * Add hardened OpenSSH client configuration defaults under
    /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/ for secure key exchange and cipher policy.
  * Add fail2ban SSH jail configuration for aggressive login throttling.
  * Add auditd tracking rules for SSH configuration and binary integrity.
  * Add AIDE monitoring rules for SSH configuration files.
  * Restrict SSH access to members of the ssh-users system group.
  * Add postinst logic to create the ssh-users group, fix SSH file
    permissions, validate configuration, and reload active services.
  * Add postrm logic to remove override permissions and validate or reload
    services during purge operations.
    (Closes: #100000)

 -- curtistinkers <curtistinkers@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
